Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override Back Button Behavior

In your `EditProductPage.xaml.cs`:

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        // Custom back button text
        Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
        {
            TextOverride = "Cancel",
            Command = new Command(async () => await OnBackRequested())
        });
    }

    // Intercept hardware/software back button
    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () => await OnBackRequested());
            return true; // Cancel default navigation
        }
        return base.OnBackButtonPressed();
    }

    private async Task OnBackRequested()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (leave)
                await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
        }
        else
        {
            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
        }
    }
}
```

## 2. Track Unsaved Changes

```csharp
// Call this when form fields change
private void OnFieldChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    _hasUnsavedChanges = true;
}
```

## Key Points

| Mechanism | What it handles |
|-----------|----------------|
| `OnBackButtonPressed()` | Android hardware back, desktop back |
| `BackButtonBehavior.Command` | Shell toolbar back button tap |
| `return true` | Cancels default navigation |

**Note:** `OnBackButtonPressed` doesn't fire on iOS swipe-back. To handle that, disable the gesture:

```csharp
Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
{
    TextOverride = "Cancel",
    Command = new Command(async () => await OnBackRequested()),
    IsVisible = true // keeps custom button visible
});

// Disable iOS swipe-back gesture on this page
Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.iOSSpecific.Page
    .SetPrefersHomeIndicatorAutoHidden(this, false);
```

Or in XAML with platform-specific config:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns:ios="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.iOSSpecific;assembly=Microsoft.Maui.Controls"
             ios:Page.UseSafeArea="True">
```

For full iOS swipe-back interception, you'd need a custom renderer or handler to disable the `InteractivePopGestureRecognizer`.
